			Real Newtonsoft.Json (not Terrasoft.NewtonsoftWrapper). The wrapper is the
			default for configuration packages but exposes only a curated subset of the
			JSON API; it omits DateParseHandling, so its reader unconditionally coerces
			date-looking argument strings (e.g. "2026-06-19T14:00:00") into DateTime and
			breaks string-typed MCP tool parameters at validation. Packages that do heavy
			JSON / LLM work (CrtCopilot, CrtCall, ...) reference the real assembly the same
			way to regain DateParseHandling. References are mutually exclusive — naming both
			collides on the Newtonsoft.Json types.
